{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"halign"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLeftCenterRight","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL18MXLLeftCenterRightO","text":"MXLLeftCenterRight"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Words and music by Pat Songwriter"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Typically this type of credit is aligned to the right, so that the position information refers to the right-"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"most part of the text. But in this example, the text is center-justified, not right-justified."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The halign attribute is used in these situations. If it is not present, its value is the same as for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"justify attribute. For elements where a justify attribute is not allowed, the default is implementation-"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dependent."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps to the MusicXML "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"halign"},{"type":"text","text":" attribute."}]}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDynamics\/halign","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Property","symbolKind":"property","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"halign"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL18MXLLeftCenterRightO","text":"MXLLeftCenterRight"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"title":"halign","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL11MXLDynamicsV6halignAA18MXLLeftCenterRightOSgvp","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"role":"symbol"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDynamics"]]},"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldynamics\/halign"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"In cases where text extends over more than one line, horizontal alignment and justify values can be different.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The most typical case is for credits, such as:","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLLeftCenterRight":{"title":"MXLLeftCenterRight","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"MXLLeftCenterRight","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlleftcenterright","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLeftCenterRight","abstract":[{"text":"The left-center-right type is used to define horizontal alignment and text justification.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLLeftCenterRight"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDynamics":{"abstract":[{"text":"Dynamics can be associated either with a note or a general musical direction. To avoid inconsistencies between","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and among the letter abbreviations for dynamics (what is sf vs. sfz, standing alone or with a trailing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dynamic that is not always piano), we use the actual letters as the names of these dynamic elements. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"other-dynamics element allows other dynamic marks that are not covered here. Dynamics elements may also be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"combined to create marks not covered by a single element, such as sfmp.","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLDynamics","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLDynamics","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLDynamics","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldynamics","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDynamics"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","type":"topic","role":"collection"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDynamics/halign":{"kind":"symbol","title":"halign","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldynamics\/halign","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"halign","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLLeftCenterRight","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL18MXLLeftCenterRightO","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDynamics\/halign","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"In cases where text extends over more than one line, horizontal alignment and justify values can be different."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The most typical case is for credits, such as:"}]}}}